MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_001: Ah, there you are. If you wanted to train, all you had\nto do was ask.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_002: Hmmm... Haaah...
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_003: {SetColor=Gray}Oh, he's meditating. Wow, talk about focus.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_004: Hmmm... Haaah...
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_005: {SetColor=Gray}Now that I get a good look at him...he is handsome.\nEspecially with those eyes closed. And mouth shut.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_006: {SetColor=Gray}What am I saying? This is no way to talk about\nsomeone who can't defend himself.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_007: {SetColor=Gray}I should probably let him be. But I could do him a\ngood turn...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_008: Hm?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_009: So you've finally opened your eyes. It's almost\nsundown. You went all day without food or drink.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_010: I've brought you a little something from my kitchen.\nEat up.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_011: I will partake of the bread, but not the coffee.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_012: You'd rather have water? But coffee goes so well\nwith this bread.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_013: Trust me, you'll like it! Just take a sip.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_014: I refuse. It is too bitter.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_015: What are you, a spoiled kid? I thought you were a\ngrown man!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_016: My daughter has been drinking my coffee since she\nwas little, you know.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_017: I tried it in Fódlan. I would rather drink\nditch water.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_018: There's no way my coffee is anything like that! Come\non, give it a try before it gets cold.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_019: Hm? This... This is remarkable.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_020: Isn't it? I tried to tell you. Nobody brews better than\nI do.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_021: My sister taught me the trick for drawing the\nsweetness out of the beans.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_022: I see. Skillful indeed.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_023: You...you charmer! Cut that out!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_024: Your smiling face, your silver tongue! I won't have it!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_025: How many men and women alike have you charmed\nwith those looks? I can see right through you!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_026: Hm.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_027: I've got to stay clear of men, not get mixed up with\none. Oof.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_028: In battle, we're allies, but that's it. I'm not interested\nin you, and you're not interested in me. Got it?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_C_029: As you wish it.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_001: Augh!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_002: Damn you! Let's see how you like THIS!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_003: Yah! Back at you!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_004: Ugh... That was one tough battle...
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_005: Foul brew...
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_006: Dietrich! You're already here? I just got back!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_007: Yes. You are late.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_008: You do realize there was a battle going on, yeah?\nI had to deal with our foes.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_009: What about you? If you were all done with yours,\nwhy not help us with ours?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_010: Hm? The dance of death is best performed as a solo.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_011: Are you kidding? If we work together, there's no foe\nthat can beat us.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_012: You have our backs, and we have yours. Isn't that\nhow it's supposed to work?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_013: I would not know. And is it not strange for you to\nsay this?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_014: You are not interested in me. I am not interested in\nyou...or so you said.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_015: Wait just a second! That isn't what I meant at all!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_016: I was talking about falling in love, not falling\nin battle!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_017: Tell me how love and battle differ. When I sight one\nworthy of a duel, my heart leaps.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_018: What in the... What's wrong with you? Ugh...\nWhat did I do to deserve this?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_019: I guess I see how you got confused, but I didn't mean\nwe shouldn't worry about each other!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_020: So you do wish for my concern? A duel to the death\nit is, then.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_021: What? No! How did you arrive at that?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_B_022: From one extreme to the other... Talking to you\nis exhausting!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_001: You're wide open! I've got you now!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_002: Ugh! Damn it!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_003: Hyah!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_004: Ahhh... If it wasn't for you, I'd be bleeding out.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_005: Pay it no mind. He flickered into my periphery.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_006: Heh. So you've been watching out for me, have\nyou? Seems like you learned to care.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_007: Glad my little lecture did its job!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_008: Now, let us away. Quickly.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_009: Something urgent? Go on ahead, and I'll catch up.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_010: No. With me, now. And then, coffee.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_011: Huh. You've developed quite a taste for it, it seems.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_012: All other coffee is vile. Yours, however,\nis exceptional.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_013: Glad to hear it. But you're exaggerating, aren't you?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_014: I am not. Other coffee brings agony with but a\nsingle drop.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_015: I see... No, wait. Dietrich... When you saved me just\nnow, was it just so I'd make you coffee?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_016: If you were lost, there would be no coffee.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_017: So you admit it! Dietrich... Listen. Your companions\nare important. Don't you understand?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_018: Why are you angry? You are important, so I\nsaved you.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_019: Because I can brew coffee! You just said as much.\nGods, look at that vacant stare. He's clueless.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_020: OK, let's try this. What if I refuse to brew a single\ncup of coffee until you learn to care about us?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_021: That would be...very difficult.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_022: Oh, that would be difficult, would it? You pick the\nstrangest times to lay your cards on the table.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_023: Tell me, then. Is there to be coffee?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_024: Ughhh... Alright, already. I'm not made of stone.\nIf you want coffee that badly...I'll make some.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_025: And this time, I'll show you how to do it as well.\nIt's not that hard!
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_026: After all, you're always forced to wait for me to do it.\nYou don't strike me as patient.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_027: I need not be shown. It is the coffee you brew that\nI crave.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_028: There's that silver tongue I was worried about! He's\nnot just a pretty face indeed.
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_029: But you won't fool me. You're just too lazy to make\nit yourself, aren't you?
MID_SE_Dit_Mic_A_030: Yes. That is true as well.